/assets/label15-1650803760846.jpg?v=1650803810" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/label15-1650803760846.jpg?v=1650803810 1536w" width="874" height="890"/></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><button type="button" aria-label="Previous" class="glider-prev glider-nav glider-nav-1"></button><button type="button" aria-label="Next" class="glider-next glider-nav glider-nav-1"></button><div class="glider-dots glider-d-1"></div></div></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:6;--c-lg:6"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-95_"><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-96_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph" data-animation="fadeInUp"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-98_"><strong>LABEL ART</strong>
<br><br>Our labels are artworks in themselves. Many of the labels were designed by winners of the Sovereign Art Foundation (SAF) prize in the year the wine was bottled. Others feature the artworks of world famous artists.<br><br>Each bottle represents more than wine — it carries a story of creativity and transformation. Through our partnership with the Sovereign Art Foundation, every purchase contributes directly to art therapy programmes supporting disadvantaged children.</span></p><a href="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/Rotulos_Aug_2026.pdf?v=1788348901" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button" data-animation="fadeInUp" class="sc-dycZeM cAZmJV pf-99_ pf-button-1 animate-grow"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-101_">Explore our labels</span></a></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-dc29" data-category="Newsletter" data-name="Clover" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-lmUbDS kbVXZM pf-102_"><div class="sc-cTTcKX dkCVVW"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-103_ pf-r pf-c-cm pf-r-eh" style="--s-lg:0px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row" data-animation="fadeInUp"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:6;--c-lg:6"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-104_"><h3 data-pf-type="Heading2" class="sc-eXrZXP kKCRVy pf-105_">More than Wine</h3><p class="sc-bkzPyv QyTch pf-107_" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">At Howard’s Folly, wine is just the beginning.Every bottle sold supports real change — funding creative programmes that empower children through art, both globally and in Portugal.When you choose Howard’s Folly, you’re not just enjoying exceptional wine — you’re becoming part of something bigger.</p></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:6;--c-lg:6"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-109_"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/kmkmmkmk.png?v=1776253437" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/kmkmmkmk.png?v=1776253437 1536w, https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/kmkmmkmk_500x.png?v=1776253437 320w" width="1920" height="1080" alt="kmkmmkmk.png__PID:eda5a9ed-1e09-4eaa-92b4-dec977a2f098" data-pf-type="Image3" class="sc-bvgOGf hzyqUz pf-110_"/></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-c537" data-pf-type="Section" data-animation="fadeInUp" id="People" class="sc-lmUbDS kbVXZM pf-111_ pf-color-scheme-1"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-cTTcKX dkCVVW"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-112_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-113_"><h1 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-bOQUxc cBnkcD pf-114_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-116_">Our People</span></h1><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-117_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-119_"><span style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Our people are passionate about winemaking and have the expertise and vision to create wines which are truly exceptional.</span></span></p><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-120_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;--s-lg:23px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-121_"><div data-pf-type="Image" class="sc-campCi jQLilF pf-122_ pf-image-1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/howard300x300-1650802869125.gif?v=1650802878" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/howard300x300-1650802869125.gif?v=1650802878 1536w" width="300" height="300"/></div><h3 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-bOQUxc cBnkcD pf-123_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-125_"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Howard Bilton</span><br><br>Co-Founder &amp; Entrepeneur</span></h3><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-126_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-128_">Howard is a businessman from Yorkshire now living in Hong Kong, an enthusiastic wine lover and admirer of Portugal’s wines especially from the Alentejo region.
<br><br>In 2002 he joined forces with David to create wines that express the best characteristics of the terroir and grape varietals.
<br><br>As the “Howard” of Howard’s Folly, he is the driving force behind the enterprise,  with a vision to promote not just our wines, but the wines of the Alentejo and Portugal to a wider global audience.</span></p></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-129_"><div data-pf-type="Image" class="sc-campCi jQLilF pf-130_ pf-image-1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/david300x300-1650802869122.gif?v=1650802875" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/david300x300-1650802869122.gif?v=1650802875 1536w" width="300" height="300"/></div><h3 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-bOQUxc cBnkcD pf-131_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-133_"><span style="font-weight: bold;">David Baverstock</span><br><br>Co-Founder &amp; Chief Winemaker</span></h3><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-134_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-136_">David has decades of experience, technical skill &amp; creativity. He is celebrated as the pioneer of modern winemaking in Portugal and is the only non-Portuguese national to win Winemaker of the Year – not once, but twice - in 2013 and 2015.<br><br>His contribution to the wine industry was uniquely recognized by the President of Portugal with the award of the Comendadorda Ordemdo Mérito Empresarial.<br><br>He is passionate about innovation, quality and unlocking the unique characteristics that each vintage offers.</span></p></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:4;--c-md:4;--c-lg:4"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-137_"><div data-pf-type="Image" class="sc-campCi jQLilF pf-138_ pf-image-1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/cristina300x300-1650802869117.gif?v=1650802870" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/t/3/assets/cristina300x300-1650802869117.gif?v=1650802870 1536w" width="300" height="300"/></div><h3 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-bOQUxc cBnkcD pf-139_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-141_"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Cristina Francisquinho</span><br><br>Vineyard Manager</span></h3><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-142_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-144_">One of the Alentejo’s best known and most respected viticulturists, Cristina was born in Portalegre.<br><br>After completing her degree in Agricultural Sciences, she worked for various grape producers and was Director of a production cooperative winery.<br><br>Her mission is to enhance the vineyards by application of sustainable agricultural and environmental practices to improve productivity and  grape quality to facilitate the production of  wines of excellence.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-04b8" data-pf-type="Section" data-animation="fadeInUp" id="People" class="sc-lmUbDS kbVXZM pf-145_ pf-color-scheme-1"><div style="--cw:1170px" class="sc-cTTcKX dkCVVW"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-146_ pf-r pf-c-ct pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;--s-lg:24px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-147_"><div data-pf-type="Tabs" class="sc-iQbOXA jgsohE pf-148_"><div data-pf-type="TabsMenu" class="sc-fIGKkh fFDuyU pf-149_"><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="true" class="sc-fEiJeM kNlhpm pf-150_ pf-anchor" data-pf-type="TabHeader"><i class="sc-fFlofg aaTDI pf-151_ pf-icon-1 pfaV4 pfaV4-circle-thin" data-pf-type="Icon"></i><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-152_">Tom Bilton<br>Managing Director </span></button><button type="button" data-pf-tab-active="false" class="sc-fEiJeM kNlhpm pf-153_ pf-anchor" data-pf-type="TabHeader"><i class="sc-fFlofg aaTDI pf-154_ pf-icon-1 pfaV4 pfaV4-circle-thin" data-pf-type="Icon"></i><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-155_">Luís Lérias<br>Winemaker<br></span></button></div><div data-pf-type="TabContentWrapper" class="sc-iA-DtKN gJkcJG pf-156_"><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:block" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-ciQpcn iWpuID pf-157_"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-158_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:6;--c-md:6;--c-lg:3"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-159_"><div data-pf-type="Image" class="sc-campCi jQLilF pf-160_ pf-image-1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/Tom_profile_pic_2.jpg?v=1759333158" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/Tom_profile_pic_2.jpg?v=1759333158 1536w" width="1170" height="1226" alt="Tom profile pic 2.jpg__PID:e3682624-cd93-429a-a53f-c265728cdf71"/></div></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:6;--c-md:6;--c-lg:9"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-161_"><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-162_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-164_">Tom started his career in the art world working for White Cube and then as an artist’s assistant. He then changed industries to work in events management and worked on BBC Countryfile Live. <br><br>Tom has always had a passion for food and wine, honed through his experience of working for his mother, a chef. He jumped at the chance of working in the wine industry and currently runs European Sales for Howard’s Folly.&nbsp;</span></p></div></div></div></div><div data-pf-expandable="true" style="display:none" data-pf-type="TabsContent" class="sc-ciQpcn iWpuID pf-165_"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-166_ pf-r pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:15px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:6;--c-md:6;--c-lg:3"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-167_"><div data-pf-type="Image" class="sc-campCi jQLilF pf-168_ pf-image-1"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/luis_profile_pic.jpg?v=1759312923" srcSet="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0608/9428/1940/files/luis_profile_pic.jpg?v=1759312923 1536w" width="1024" height="1024" alt="luis profile pic.jpg__PID:a65d1010-9dfb-4476-8c2c-b42b13b07d43"/></div></div></div><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:6;--c-md:6;--c-lg:9"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-169_"><p class="sc-eBwJYS dJbEKt pf-170_ pf-text-1" data-pf-type="Paragraph"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-172_">Luís, Alentejo born and raised, comes from a family with strong ties to agriculture, so his career progression was somewhat easy to predict. At the Santarém Agricultural College, he found his true calling: the world of wine, and the desire to make art out of what nature gives us.
<br>He has worked on projects across the Alentejo, Tejo, and Lisbon regions, where he not only gained valuable experience but also cultivated a meticulous attention to detail and a spirit of boldness that have allowed him to craft wines of true distinction. “Bringing the São Mamede mountains to tables around the world has always been a dream, and at Howard’s Folly it has become reality in the most artistic way possible.”</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-section-id="pf-e456" data-pf-type="Section" class="sc-lmUbDS kbVXZM pf-173_ pf-color-scheme-1"><div class="sc-cTTcKX dkCVVW"><div class="sc-hZDzol kRuHOG pf-174_ pf-r pf-c-cm pf-r-eh" style="--s-xs:0px;position:relative" data-pf-type="Row"><div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs:12;--c-sm:12;--c-md:12;--c-lg:12"><div data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-ezrfit gUxRQT pf-175_"><h1 data-pf-type="Heading" class="sc-bOQUxc cBnkcD pf-176_ pf-heading-1-h3"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-178_"><font color="#ffffff">Howard's Folly Winery</font></span></h1><a href="/pages/our-winery-howards-folly" target="_self" data-pf-type="Button" class="sc-dycZeM cAZmJV pf-179_ pf-button-1"><span data-pf-type="Text" class="sc-kuVMvl bBmUMO pf-181_">Explore</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><script>
